@node InitHook
@prev Author
@next main
@toc main

@{b}InitHook@{ub}

@{b}   NAME@{ub}
	InitHook -- Hook Setup
@{b}   SYNOPSIS@{ub}
	BOOLEAN InitHook( *ClassPtr.IClass, DispatcherAdr.l )
@{b}   RESULT@{ub}
	result - Hook setup result ( True or False )
@{b}   EXAMPLE@{ub}
        Note: Your class has to be been opened first!
        You could write:

	InitHook *Class, ?Dispatcher or if ...
	....( Program routine suite )
        ....
        ....
        End

        Note: Your dispatcher should always goes after everything
              NEVER IN A FUNCTION OR STATEMENT

        Dispatcher
             ...
             ...
        RTS


@{" Back to Main " link main}
@endnode



@node GetHookMsg
@prev InitHook
@next main
@toc main

@{b}GetHookMsg/GetHookObj@{ub}

@{b}   NAME@{ub}
	GetHookMsg/GetHookObj -- Get important Hook Pointers
@{b}   SYNOPSIS@{ub}
	*Ptr.(Msg/_Object) = GetHookXXX
@{b}   RESULT@{ub}
	result - Information from the Hook/Dispatcher
@{b}   EXAMPLE@{ub}
       Note: Those commands should always go in the Dispatcher.

       Dispatcher
           *MsgPtr.Msg = GetHookMsg
           *ObjPtr.l   = GetHookObj
            
           Select *Msg\Method
                Case #OM_NEW
                *o = DoSuperMethodA( *ClassPtr, *ObjPtr, &MsgPtr )
           ....
           end Select
       
       ....
       ....
       RTS
        

@{" Back to Main " link main}
@endnode


@node Inst_Data
@prev GetHookMsg
@next main
@toc main

@{b}INST_DATA@{ub}

       Note:
       This is missing macro from the Includes( intuition/classes.h )
       This function add offset for instance data to an objet handle.

@{b}   NAME@{ub}
	*Ptr Newtype.( Boopsi Gadget info ) = INST_DATA( *Class.Iclass, *o )
        Note: *o = object handle from DoSuperMethodA...

@{b}   SYNOPSIS@{ub}
	*Ptr.Struct = INST_DATA( *Class, *o )
@{b}   RESULT@{ub}
	result - Address of the TagsList 
@{b}   EXAMPLE@{ub}
       Note: Those commands should always go in the Dispatcher.

       Dispatcher
           *MsgPtr.Msg = GetHookMsg
           *ObjPtr.l   = GetHookObj
            
           Select *Msg\Method
                Case #OM_NEW
                     *o = DoSuperMethodA( *ClassPtr, *ObjPtr, &MsgPtr )
                      if *o
                         *DT.Struct = INST_DATA( *Class, *o )
                         ....
                         Note: very useful for the GetTagData_ 

           end Select
       
       ....
       ....
       RTS

@{" Back to Main " link main}
@endnode

@NODE DoMethod "Amiga_Lib"

@{fg shine}Command: DoMethod@{fg text}
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Modes  : 
Syntax : DoMethod(Obj,MethodID,Tag[,Tag..])

Execute the method 'MethodID' on the object 'Obj'.

@ENDNODE DoMethod

@NODE DoMethodA "Amiga_Lib"

@{fg shine}Command: DoMethodA@{fg text}
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Modes  : 
Syntax : DoMethodA(Obj,Msg)

Same as DoMethod but with a Tag structure as argument.



@ENDNODE DoMethodA

@NODE DoSuperMethod "Amiga_Lib"

@{fg shine}Command: DoSuperMethod@{fg text}
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Modes  : 
Syntax : DoSuperMethod(Class,Obj,MethodID,Tag[,Tag..])

Execute the method 'MethodID' on the object 'Obj' and from the superclass
'Class'.

@ENDNODE DoSuperMethod

@NODE DoSuperMethodA "Amiga_Lib"

@{fg shine}Command: DoSuperMethodA@{fg text}
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Modes  : 
Syntax : DoSuperMethodA(Class,Obj,Msg)

Same as DoSuperMethod but with a Tag structure as argument.



@ENDNODE DoSuperMethodA

@NODE CoerceMethod "Amiga_Lib"

@{fg shine}Command: CoerceMethod@{fg text}
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Modes  : 
Syntax : CoerceMethod(Class,Obj,MethodID,Tag[,Tag..])

Execute the method 'MethodID' on the coerced object 'Obj' and from the class
'Class'.



@ENDNODE CoerceMethod

@NODE CoerceMethodA "Amiga_Lib"

@{fg shine}Command: CoerceMethodA@{fg text}
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Modes  : 
Syntax : CoerceMethodA(Class,Obj,MethodID,Msg)

Same as CoerceMethod but with a Tag structure as argument.



@ENDNODE CoerceMethod

@NODE SetSuperAttrs "Amiga_Lib"

@{fg shine}Command: SetSuperAttrs@{fg text}
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Modes  : 
Syntax : SetSuperAttrs(Class,Obj,Tag[,Tag..])

Change settings of the superclass 'Class' of the object 'Obj'.



@ENDNODE SetSuperAttrs

@NODE VarArgs "Amiga_Lib"

@{fg shine}Function: VarArgs@{fg text}
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Modes  : 
Syntax : VarArgs(Tag[,Tag..])

Allow you to replace a tag structure.

Example : 
---------

  Before : 
  ~~~~~~~~
  
  NEWTYPE.tags a.l:b:c:d:e:f:g:h:i:j:k:l:m:n:o:p:q:r:s:t:u:v:w:x:y:z:End NEWTYPE
  
  DEFTYPE.tags tags
  
  tags\a=#A_TAG,var,0
  
  MyCommand_ *obj,tags
  
  After (now) :
  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  
  MyCommand_ *obj,VarArgs(#A_TAG,var,0)
  
  
  
  It's very easier and shorter!


@ENDNODE VarArgs